Title: [Bugfix][KV Cache] Zero whole storage blocks of virtually paged compressed caches

Branch: Peuqui:pr-kv-zeroer-virtual-pages (base 1Cat main 022349e47, one commit 6e3919e0b9)

----- Text -----

Fixes #1330

Problem: KVBlockZeroer (vllm/v1/worker/utils.py, _resolve_zeroer_kernel_layout and KVBlockZeroer.init_meta) assumes that the cache view of a compressed spec (storage_block_size != block_size) has one page per storage block: it returned kernel_block_size = storage_block_size and ratio = 1. The GLM-5.x kpool indexer cache is a paged-MQA cache. Its view is cut into 64-row virtual pages inside each storage block (the indexer translates the shared block table into pages), so a storage block spans several view pages. Zeroing block id b therefore cleared view page b, which belongs to block b // pages_per_block and can hold the index keys of a running request, while the pages of block b itself stayed dirty. This is the bug reported in #1330 by squibloads, who traced it on GLM-5.3-Flash with MTP 3 (page 24, a part of block 2, zeroed when block 24 was allocated for the next chunk; the 64 pooled index keys of that page lost their scale bytes) and verified a local fix.

Why it matters: the effect depends on which block ids a request holds when other blocks are allocated, so it shows as run-to-run variation (in the report: the first-token logprob of the same prompt differing between four cold requests in one engine, and record-lookup retrieval at 23 of 24 instead of 24 of 24). The pages of block b itself were not visible as a problem in the report because they are written before they are read.

Change:
- vllm/v1/worker/utils.py: new kv_cache_view_page_rows(spec, group_kernel_block_size, backend), the single place that says how many rows one page of a group's cache view has: the group's kernel block size for normal specs, the whole storage block for backends with a physical block table (for example the QSA side caches), the paged-MQA virtual page size (compressed_kernel_block_size) otherwise. This is the decision the V1 runner, the V2 runner and the metadata builder already made at three separate places.
- _resolve_zeroer_kernel_layout now takes the backend, uses kv_cache_view_page_rows and returns (page rows, pages per storage block), so the zeroer clears every page of the block id (pages_per_block pages). For physical block tables and normal specs the result is unchanged.
- vllm/v1/worker/gpu/attn_utils.py (_reshape_kv_cache), vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py (kv cache reshape) and AttentionGroup.create_metadata_builders call kv_cache_view_page_rows instead of repeating the physical-block-table decision, so the view shape, the builder spec and the zeroer cannot drift apart again. The metadata builder result is unchanged: the physical block table case was already handled before that branch.
This follows the suggestion in the issue (let the view report its page rows and derive the zeroer layout from it) instead of patching the span after the fact.

Not checked: whether the DeepSeek-V4 compressed caches use virtual-page views (the reporter did not check either). If they do, this change applies to them as well, since they go through the same zeroer code.

Tests, CPU only (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES empty; the GPU is busy with production), on main 022349e47 plus this commit, run with pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider:
- New tests in tests/v1/worker/test_kv_block_zeroer.py: test_resolve_zeroer_kernel_layout gets a virtual-page case (storage block of 256 rows, 64-row pages, expects 64 rows and 4 pages) and passes the backend; test_compressed_virtual_pages_zero_every_page_of_the_block (zeroing block 1 must clear exactly the view pages 4 to 7) and test_compressed_physical_block_table_zeroes_one_storage_block (the physical block table case stays one page per block). With the three source files of main and the new test file, 5 of the 22 tests fail; test_compressed_virtual_pages_zero_every_page_of_the_block fails on behavior ("assert 16 == 4": the old layout counts the 64-row pages as blocks), the other four fail because the old _resolve_zeroer_kernel_layout does not take a backend. With the fix: 13 passed, 9 skipped (the 9 skipped tests need CUDA).
- tests/v1/worker/test_utils.py 3 passed, test_glm5_compressed_kv_cache.py 2 passed, test_qsa_physical_kv_cache.py 12 passed, test_release_cleanup.py 5 passed, tests/v1/attention/test_gdn_metadata_builder.py 89 passed 27 skipped, tests/v1/core/test_qwen4_exp_kv_cache.py 31 passed, tests/v1/worker/test_kv_block_copy.py 6 skipped, tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_qsa_dcp_packed_cache.py 2 skipped.
- These files fail the same way on plain main 022349e47 and with this commit (identical lists of failed tests and errors, compared test by test): tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner.py (9 failed, 17 passed, 17 errors; "No CUDA GPUs are available"), test_gpu_model_runner_v2_kv_zero.py (1 failed, 3 passed: the test fake lacks decode_ckpt_mounts), test_gpu_model_runner_v2_prefill_dispatch.py (1 failed, 38 passed), test_host_kv_cache_pool.py (1 failed, 1 passed, 1 skipped), tests/models/qwen4_exp/test_qsa_cache.py (7 failed, 7 passed). I did not touch them. test_gpu_model_runner.py needs a GPU and covers the V1 runner reshape that this change edits (test_init_kv_cache_with_kv_sharing_valid and others); I could not run it here.
- pre-commit run --files on the four changed files: all hooks passed (including ruff-check, ruff-format, typos, check-torch-cuda-call). pre-commit run mypy-3.10 --hook-stage manual --files on the same files: passed.
- Not run on a GPU: the nine CUDA tests of test_kv_block_zeroer.py and the GPU-dependent tests listed above. I did not reproduce the retrieval and logprob effects from the issue on my own hardware; those numbers are the reporter's.

Not a duplicate: gh issue view 1330 shows the issue open with no comments. Searches over open and all pull requests (1330 in:body, zeroer, KVBlockZeroer, kv block zero, storage block virtual page, kv_cache_view_page_rows, indexer zero block) find only merged work on other cases of the zeroer (#276, #280, #373, #406, #1230, #1232), none that changes the page span for virtually paged caches; among the 94 open pull requests none changes _resolve_zeroer_kernel_layout, compressed_kernel_block_size or the zeroer layout. #1589 edits other code in the same files (hot block invalidation in vllm/v1/worker/utils.py), in different hunks.

AI assistance (Claude) was used; the change was reviewed and tested by the submitter.
